<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#ivory-trade">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ivory trade</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as ivory</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The ivory trade is the commerce in elephant tusks, prized for carving and luxury goods. African ivory was traded for thousands of years, from the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aksumite-empire">Aksumite Empire</a> to later states. It was important to the economies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luba-empire">Luba</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi</a> empires, among others.</p></div>
